From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 05:34:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 47/76] flashnext cuda: sum MoE slots in owner order; --tp 2
 exchanges one hidden-size row a layer

Each owner's slots (routed experts below or from 256, the shared slot's column halves) are summed as
one fma chain in slot order, then added once, in fn_moe_sum and both MoE writebacks. At --tp 2 with
the shared expert split by columns, each rank sums its own owner's chain and one FP32 all-reduce of
the hidden rows adds the other's, so TP2 keeps TP1's bits while sending 10 KiB a row a layer.
